  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unseasonably mild and dry weather will continue \nuntil late Wednesday Night.\n\nThe close proximity of a surface high to our southeast will \nkeep winds light from the SE or South and weather tranquil until\nWednesday. A sprinkle isn't out of the question later tonight \ninto tomorrow in the northern tier of counties but any \nappreciable precipitation looks to remain north of the NY \nborder. \n\nUpper level ridging builds back into the region for the first \nhalf of this week, helping to prolong our dry stretch and \nkeeping temperatures 10 to 15 degrees above normal for much\nof week. Highs in the lower 70s are in store for all but the \nhigher elevations on Wed. As a weakening low pressure system\napproached from the west along with an upper level closed low,\nthe tightening pressure gradient may allow for stronger\nsoutherly winds on Wednesday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Periods of showers preceding and accompanying a \ncold frontal passage. Cooler and a return to mainly dry \nconditions will follow for Friday through Sunday. \n\nChances for widespread rainfall return for the second half of\nthe week. Very late Wed night is the earliest anyone will see \nprecip as a complex system develops over the middle of the \ncountry. There is still uncertainty regarding exactly how this\nsystem pans out with a few phasing jets to keep track of. The\ntheme in this morning's solutions was the vertical stacking that\nbecame apparent as this system moves towards us. The main \nsurface low moves under the center of the upper level low before\nimpacting us and begins to weaken/occlude as it loses the best \nascent. With a possibly more diffuse, but still apparent,\nboundary a more stratiform precipitation mode may be favored \nwith a few heavier pockets possible. \n\nGFS and ECMWF disagree on the degree of how far a shortwave\ntrough swings down from Canada on Friday. Should a more \nprogressive solution develop, this may sweep through another \ncold front and round of precipitation Friday into Saturday. \nRegardless, long range guidance hints at cooler temperatures \nthis weekend trending more seasonable with dry conditions on the\nback of the weekend.",
